WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
In 2022, a tonne of cocoa
beans sold for about

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.210
2,400 dollars on world markets.

3
00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:12.690
By 2024, the average price
was about 7,400 dollars.

4
00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:14.550
It had more than tripled.

5
00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:17.260
And cocoa is what chocolate is made from.

6
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.980
So what decides the price of cocoa beans,

7
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.180
and why did it more than
triple in two years?

8
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.230
In this mission, you'll find the
price where buyers and sellers agree,

9
00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.990
and see what happens
when the price is wrong.

10
00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:33.090
Then you'll shift demand
and supply in the graph lab,

11
00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.590
and predict where the price goes next.

12
00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:38.630
Your mission: find out what moves a price,

13
00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.590
and what that price moves in turn.
